# Mobile Layout

When the user says **"Mobile layout"**, work in this module — not scattered media queries.

## Source of truth

- Breakpoints: `src/layout/mobile/breakpoints.ts`
- Mode resolution: `src/layout/mobile/resolve.ts`
- DOM attrs: `data-layout-mode`, `data-layout-orientation`, `data-layout-chrome` (`compact`|`wide`), `data-layout-bp`, `data-layout-surface`
- Mobile detection: `min(width, height) < 640` (landscape phones stay mobile)
- Compact chrome: mobile + tablet portrait → bottom nav, drawer, overflow guards
- CSS: `src/app/mobile-layout.css` + `mobile-layout-pages.css` (classes prefixed `ml-`)
- Hook: `useMobileLayout()` — only when JS must branch (drawers, mounts)

## Do

- Use `html[data-layout-mode="mobile"]` for responsive CSS
- Scope surface-specific rules with `data-layout-surface="admin|public|platform"`
- Reuse `ADMIN_PRIMARY_TABS` for admin navigation
- Wrap app areas in `MobileShell`

## Don't

- Add new arbitrary breakpoints (639px, 900px) without aligning to `LAYOUT_BREAKPOINTS`
- Use `useMobileLayout` for styling that CSS can handle
- Mix layout mode with `data-display-profile` (density vs shell chrome)
- Put mobile shell CSS in random feature CSS files — extend `mobile-layout.css` or page CSS with `data-layout-mode` selectors

